WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.487
This slide focuses on Use logging instead of only
print Start with the meaning of

00:00:05.513 --> 00:00:12.089
the idea then connect it to the example and the
larger analytical workflow Logging

00:00:12.116 --> 00:00:19.845
records what happened It can include messages for
progress warnings and errors Before

00:00:19.871 --> 00:00:25.624
running the example predict the output Run it in the
browser inspect the result then

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:31.413
modify one input expression or value and run it
again Notice whether the shorter

00:00:31.426 --> 00:00:34.887
technique improves clarity or only makes the code
harder to read
